      "release_id": "chatgpt-2026-10-15-applications-for-the-rosalind-academic-plan-b85717ef",
      "product": "chatgpt",
      "product_name": "ChatGPT",
      "date": "2026-10-15",
      "version": "Applications for the Rosalind Academic Plan",
      "title": "Applications for the Rosalind Academic Plan",
      "body": "The Rosalind Academic Plan helps eligible academic labs use ChatGPT for life sciences research. Approved labs can receive up to 30 ChatGPT Business Standard seats at no cost for up to 12 months, with GPT-Rosalind access subject to trusted-access approval.\nApplications are now open to labs at U.S. universities. If you’re a principal investigator or lab lead, apply on behalf of your lab. Applying doesn’t give your lab immediate access. After approval, follow the instructions to set up your workspace and enable access for approved members. Labs covered by an OpenAI Enterprise agreement should use their university’s access process. For eligibility and setup details, see: Rosalind Academic Plan.",
      "source_summary": "The Rosalind Academic Plan helps eligible academic labs use ChatGPT for life sciences research. Approved labs can receive up to 30 ChatGPT Business Standard seats at no cost for up to 12 months, with GPT-Rosalind access subject to trusted-access approval.",
      "source_url": "https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes#applications-for-the-rosalind-academic-plan",
      "source_type": "chatgpt_changelog"
    },
    {
      "release_id": "chatgpt-2026-10-15-gpt-live-1-1-and-new-voices-in-chatgpt-3e3f7f0c",
      "product": "chatgpt",
      "product_name": "ChatGPT",
      "date": "2026-10-15",
      "version": "GPT-Live-1.1 and new voices in ChatGPT",
      "title": "GPT-Live-1.1 and new voices in ChatGPT",
      "body": "We’re rolling out GPT-Live-1.1 and GPT-Live-1.1 Quip, a mini version of the model, in ChatGPT Voice, with more natural accents across languages. Live also uses a wider range of short phrases to let you know when it’s searching.\nNew Live voices include options for French, German, Hindi, Japanese, Korean, and Mexican Spanish, plus Bubbie in English. The voices you see may vary by region and account.\nTo choose a voice, open Settings > Voice, then select Voice.\nFor more information, see: ChatGPT Voice.",
      "source_summary": "We’re rolling out GPT-Live-1.1 and GPT-Live-1.1 Quip, a mini version of the model, in ChatGPT Voice, with more natural accents across languages. Live also uses a wider range of short phrases to let you know when it’s searching.",
      "source_url": "https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes#gpt-live-11-and-new-voices-in-chatgpt",
      "source_type": "chatgpt_changelog"
    },
